<h2 id="mindfulness-and-integrative-psychiatry"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Mindfulness and Integrative Psychiatry</span></h2>
<span style="font-weight: 400;">Mindfulness is an important part of an integrative care plan. Some scholars call it a “must-have” to keep our brains healthy.</span><span style="font-weight: 400;"> We’re excited to see more patients experience the benefits of mindfulness because it’s a free, accessible tool for everyone. All it takes is some personal discipline, and a few minutes to get started. </span>

&nbsp;

<span style="font-weight: 400;">If you made it all the way to the end of this article — </span><b>we invite you to take a deep breath.</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> </span>

&nbsp;

<span style="font-weight: 400;">Feel your heartbeat, and be thankful for it. Notice any sounds around you, and take a moment to register your own thoughts. Are you feeling anxious? Excited? Taking a moment for mindfulness can be as simple as this. </span>

